    {
      "name": "Is_Critical",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.55,
      "source_groundedness": 0.3,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "A criticality flag is a reasonable axis for triage analysis, and the table has a 'priority' column that could ground it. However, the distribution is heavily skewed (424 of 500 = 1), making it near-constant and low-leverage. The evidence samples reveal groundedness problems: 'Printer not working properly' and routine printer issues are labeled Is_Critical=1, which is not warranted by the source text and appears to contradict any sensible criticality reading. All five samples are '1', consistent with an over-asserting, poorly grounded flag."
    },
    {
      "name": "Resolution_Speed",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.8,
      "source_groundedness": 0.2,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Bucketing resolution time is genuinely useful for analyzing incident handling and gives a real axis to compare on. But the source evidence undermines the values badly: in every sample, sys_updated_on equals closed_at to the same timestamp, implying a resolution duration of effectively zero, yet rows are labeled 'Medium (4-10 days)', 'Slow (>10 days)', and 'Fast (≤3 days)'. The bucket assignments are not derivable from (and contradict) the timestamps shown, indicating fabricated durations."
    },
    {
      "name": "Is_Printer_Related",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A printer-related flag is a plausible, well-balanced (298/202) categorical axis for grouping incidents by theme, useful for this exploratory query. Values are soundly derived from short_description: printer descriptions map to 1, connectivity/database map to 0. Well grounded across all samples."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.68,
  "source_groundedness": 0.42,
  "rationale": "The added columns propose reasonable analytical axes (criticality, resolution speed, printer theme) that would help exploratory triage of incident tickets, so usefulness is moderate-to-good, though Is_Critical is weakened by a near-constant skew. Groundedness is the main failure: Resolution_Speed contradicts the source timestamps (updated=closed implies ~0 duration yet varied speed buckets are assigned), and Is_Critical over-asserts criticality on routine printer tickets without textual support. Only Is_Printer_Related is reliably grounded."
}

